## Summary

The derived memo metadata is computed by a **markdown AST walk** in the `internal/markdown` package, driven through a `RebuildMemoPayload` helper.

### 1. Where it is COMPUTED from content

**Core computation:** `/bench/home/work/internal/markdown/markdown.go`

There are two methods that both compute the `MemoPayload_Property` by parsing content into a goldmark AST and walking it:

- **`(*service).ExtractProperties`** — lines **192-241** (properties only)
- **`(*service).ExtractAll`** — lines **355-406+** (tags, mentions, AND properties in a single parse — this is the one actually used by the rebuild path)

The extraction logic (from `ExtractAll`, lines 371-406):
```go
// Check if the first block-level child of the document is an H1 heading.
if !firstBlockChecked && n.Parent() != nil && n.Parent().Kind() == gast.KindDocument {
    firstBlockChecked = true
    if heading, ok := n.(*gast.Heading); ok && heading.Level == 1 {
        data.Property.Title = extractHeadingText(n, content)
    }
}

switch n.Kind() {
case gast.KindLink:
    data.Property.HasLink = true
case gast.KindCodeBlock, gast.KindFencedCodeBlock, gast.KindCodeSpan:
    data.Property.HasCode = true
case east.KindTaskCheckBox:
    data.Property.HasTaskList = true
    if checkBox, ok := n.(*east.TaskCheckBox); ok {
        if !checkBox.IsChecked {
            data.Property.HasIncompleteTasks = true
        }
    }
}
```

**Wiring/entry point:** `/bench/home/work/server/runner/memopayload/runner.go`, function **`RebuildMemoPayload`** (lines **74-88**). This is the single site that stamps the computed data onto the memo:
```go
func RebuildMemoPayload(_ context.Context, memo *store.Memo, markdownService markdown.Service) error {
	if memo.Payload == nil {
		memo.Payload = &storepb.MemoPayload{}
	}
	data, err := markdownService.ExtractAll([]byte(memo.Content))
	if err != nil {
		return errors.Wrap(err, "failed to extract markdown metadata")
	}
	memo.Payload.Tags = data.Tags
	memo.Payload.Property = data.Property
	return nil
}
```

### 2. Operations that TRIGGER recomputation

Callers of `RebuildMemoPayload` (grep confirmed these are the only ones):

- **CreateMemo** — `/bench/home/work/server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:108`. Called on the `create` object before `s.Store.CreateMemo`.
- **UpdateMemo** — `/bench/home/work/server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:447`. Called only when the `content` field is in the update mask (`contentUpdated` branch, lines 436-451); the recomputed `memo.Payload` is written via `update.Payload = memo.Payload`.
- **Batch rebuild / migration** — `/bench/home/work/server/runner/memopayload/runner.go:52`, inside `(*Runner).RunOnce` (lines 27-72). This iterates all memos in batches of 100, calls `RebuildMemoPayload`, then `Store.UpdateMemo` with the new payload.

Note on the batch runner: `RunOnce`/`NewRunner` are defined but **not currently wired into server startup** (`server.go` only calls the s3presign runner's `RunOnce`; grep found no non-test caller of `memopayload.NewRunner` or `RunOnce`). So in the running server, recomputation is triggered only by CreateMemo and content-updating UpdateMemo. The `Runner` exists as an on-demand/migration rebuild-all mechanism.

### 3. Extracted fields

Written into `storepb.MemoPayload` (proto struct at `/bench/home/work/proto/gen/store/memo.pb.go`):

- **`Payload.Tags`** — `[]string` of `#tags` (from `asMemoTagNode`).
- **`Payload.Property`** (`MemoPayload_Property`):
  - **`HasLink`** (bool) — any markdown link node.
  - **`HasCode`** (bool) — any code block, fenced code block, or inline code span.
  - **`HasTaskList`** (bool) — any task checkbox.
  - **`HasIncompleteTasks`** (bool) — any unchecked task checkbox.
  - **`Title`** (string) — text of the document's first block-level child if it is an H1 heading.

These properties are surfaced to the API via `convertMemoPropertyFromStore` at `/bench/home/work/server/router/api/v1/memo_service_converter.go:314-325`, mapping the store property to the `v1pb.Memo_Property` used in list/preview responses.

